      "side": 1,
      "message": "We probably want to return an error in this case since initialize was not called (e.g. ScopedAStatus::fromExceptionCode(EX_ILLEGAL_STATE))\n\nOne possible suggestion - switch \u0027send\u0027 to return ndk::ScopedAStatus. For instance in the header: \"[[nodiscard]] ndk::ScopedAStatus send(PacketType type, const std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e\u0026 v);\" - the [[nodiscard]] makes sure all users of it will check the state. Then the above functions could be \"return send(...)\" and you would only need one check.\n\nA zero-size packet should probably return EX_ILLEGAL_ARGUMENT, especially because we know it shouldn\u0027t be sent otherwise.",
